-- title:
--   Canonical-subgroup sorting of Uₚ at a place of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$.
--
--   *Cyclotomic base data.* $L$ is a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ with $K = \mathrm{ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange}\, L\, (\mathrm{ModularCurve.x1FunctionField}\,(Mp))$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   *Coefficient ring.* $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ forming a scalar tower with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is assumed non-zero and to have Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), so that $j$ is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. The associated finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ is the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element $\mathrm{jChartFin} = j$; $\mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$ is the pushout of the two chart inclusions, $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (assumed proper), and $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$ the chart morphism from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra into the two-chart model.
--
--   *Mod $p$ fibre data.* $k$ is an algebraically closed $A$-algebra of characteristic $p$, and $C_1, C_2$ are schemes, proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ via $c_1, c_2$, equipped with morphisms $i_1, i_2$ over the base change of $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ to $k$ whose underlying scheme morphisms are closed immersions; the hypothesis `hcover` requires every point of the pullback of $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ to lie in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, `hred` requires the pullback of $i_1$ and $i_2$ to be reduced, and $n$ is a positive natural number equal to the cardinality of that pullback.
--
--   *Generic fibre identification.* $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structures make $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the algebraic closure `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) an $A$- and an $L$-algebra in a scalar tower. $M_\eta$ is a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp) = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))$, that is, an integral scheme $M_\eta.C$ proper and smooth of relative dimension one over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with an isomorphism of its function field with that field, compatible with the structure map, and a bijection `placeOfPoint` of its closed points with the places of the field, whose local rings match the valuation subrings; `pointEquivPlace` is the induced bijection between $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-sections of $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ and places. Further, $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism of $M_\eta.C$ with the pullback of $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, with $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection equal to $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`heη`). The preimage under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the top open under $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$ is assumed non-empty as a scheme. The pinning hypothesis `hMηpin` requires that for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra the element of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ obtained by transporting $a$ to sections over the chart image, restricting along $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection, taking the germ at the generic point, and applying the inverse of $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$, has Laurent series equal to the image of the Laurent series of $a$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) of $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The equivariance hypothesis `hgal` requires that for every $g \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-sections $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by $x$, $e_\eta$ and the first projection, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}(x') = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))(g) \cdot M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}(x)$, the action being that of the semilinear automorphism acting coefficientwise on Laurent series.
--
--   *The second $j$-value.* $j_p$ is an element of the finite chart algebra whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p\,(\mathrm{jq})$, i.e. of $j(q^p)$.
--
--   *Place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and residue data.* $P\!l$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P\!l$; $\rho : A \to P\!l$ is a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $P\!l \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map of $A$; and $\pi_k : P\!l \to k$ is a ring homomorphism with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$.
--
--   *Hecke data.* `hβdef` asserts that for every $y$ in $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp)$ the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p\,y$ lies in $\mathrm{x1x0FunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,(Mp)\,(Mp\cdot p)$; `hα` and `hβ` assert that the two maps $\mathrm{heckeAlphaOneBar}$ (the inclusion of $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp))$ into $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1x0FunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,(Mp)\,(Mp\cdot p))$) and $\mathrm{heckeBetaOneBar}$ (which, `hβdef` holding, is the map induced by $q \mapsto q^p$) are integral; the field $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{x1x0FunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,(Mp)\,(Mp\cdot p))$ is assumed to have principal divisors over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and `hdeg` assumes $\mathrm{finrankAlong}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{heckeBetaOneBar}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(Mp)\,p) = p$. The correspondence $\mathrm{heckeDivOneBar}\,h\alpha\,h\beta$ on divisors of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ is pullback along $\mathrm{heckeBetaOneBar}$ followed by pushforward along $\mathrm{heckeAlphaOneBar}$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every place $P$ of $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every ring homomorphism $\psi$ from the finite chart algebra to $P\!l$ such that
--
--   (i) $\psi \circ (A \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j) = \rho$;
--
--   (ii) $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $P\!l \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ composed with $\psi$, followed by $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$, equals the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-section $(\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}P)$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection;
--
--   (iii) $(\pi_k \circ \psi)(\mathrm{jChartFin}) = ((\pi_k \circ \psi)(j_p))^p$;
--
--   (iv) $((\pi_k \circ \psi)(\mathrm{jChartFin}))^{p^2} \neq (\pi_k \circ \psi)(\mathrm{jChartFin})$;
--
--   there exist a place $Q_p$, a ring homomorphism $\psi_p$ from the finite chart algebra to $P\!l$, a family $Q : \mathrm{Fin}(p-1) \to$ places and a family $\psi_Q : \mathrm{Fin}(p-1) \to$ ring homomorphisms from the finite chart algebra to $P\!l$ with the following three properties.
--
--   First, $\mathrm{heckeDivOneBar}\,h\alpha\,h\beta$ applied to the divisor $\mathrm{single}\,P\,1$ equals $\mathrm{single}\,Q_p\,1 + \sum_{i : \mathrm{Fin}(p-1)} \mathrm{single}\,(Q\,i)\,1$.
--
--   Secondly, $\psi_p$ satisfies the four conditions: $\psi_p \circ (A \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j) = \rho$; $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $P\!l \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ composed with $\psi_p$, followed by $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$, equals the section $(\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}Q_p)$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection; $(\pi_k \circ \psi_p)(\mathrm{jChartFin}) = ((\pi_k \circ \psi_p)(j_p))^p$; and $((\pi_k \circ \psi_p)(\mathrm{jChartFin}))^{p^2} \neq (\pi_k \circ \psi_p)(\mathrm{jChartFin})$.
--
--   Thirdly, for each $i : \mathrm{Fin}(p-1)$: $\psi_Q\,i$ composed with $A \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ equals $\rho$; $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $P\!l \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ composed with $\psi_Q\,i$, followed by $\mathrm{ιFin}\,A\,K\,j$, equals the section $(\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}(Q\,i))$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection; the congruence holds in the reversed direction, $(\pi_k \circ \psi_Q\,i)(j_p) = ((\pi_k \circ \psi_Q\,i)(\mathrm{jChartFin}))^p$; and $((\pi_k \circ \psi_Q\,i)(\mathrm{jChartFin}))^{p^2} \neq (\pi_k \circ \psi_Q\,i)(\mathrm{jChartFin})$.
--
--   No disjointness or distinctness of $Q_p$ and the $Q\,i$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the place-by-place form of the Kronecker congruence $\Phi_p(X,Y) \equiv (X^p - Y)(X - Y^p) \bmod p$ for the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$: a point whose reduction satisfies $j \equiv j_p^{\,p}$ and lies off the $\mathbb{F}_{p^2}$-locus of $j$ has its $U_p$-image split into one point obeying the same congruence and $p-1$ points obeying the opposite one. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the mod $p$ fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ and of the reduction of the $U_p$ correspondence, being used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finset_heckeDivOneBar_single_eq_single_add_sum_of_red_notMem_of_reducesSnd_of_gaussReading_snd_algEquiv_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_finset_heckeDivOneBar_single_eq_single_add_sum_of_red_notMem_of_reducesSnd_of_gaussReading_snd_algEquiv_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
